gs platform serves as a bridge between users and the refrigerator, offering both in-person control via the touch panel and remote management through a dedicated app available on Google Play Store, Galaxy Apps, or Apple App Store. Users can access a specialized mode by long-pressing the circle button on the control panel to get detailed status updates or advanced settings [Data: Entities (25, 681, 26, 641); Relationships (744, 793, 774)]. However, app availability may be affected by operating system policy changes, potentially making it difficult to download or update [Data: Entities (26)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"AI Energy Saving Mode optimizes power usage but may reduce cooling performance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The AI Energy Saving Mode is a feature available in the SmartThings application that can be turned on or off to reduce energy consumption. While this mode helps with energy efficiency, it may lead to decreased cooling performance, which users should consider when preserving sensitive food items. Some refrigerator models display an icon on the main panel to indicate the mode is active [Data: Entities (732, 681); Relationships (841)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Wireless network connectivity relies on specific protocols and security standards\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Samsung smart refrigerator supports IEEE 802.11 b/g/n wireless protocols operating at 2.4 GHz, with IEEE 802.11 n being the recommended protocol for optimal performance. The device requires encryption systems such as WPA/TKIP and WPA2/AES for network security, and warns that newer or non-standard authentication protocols are not supported. Unauthorized Wi-Fi routers may fail to connect, and the surrounding wireless environment can affect network performance [Data: Entities (692, 691, 699, 695, 696, 700, 701); Relationships (802, 800, 805, 797, 801, 803, 804)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Control panel user interface supports accessibility for hearing-impaired users\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The control panel is designed to stay in sleep mode when not in use, activating only when the door is opened or a button is tapped. An internal indicator light blinks for 5 minutes if the door is open for that duration, specifically designed to alert deaf and hard-of-hearing users [Data: Entities (654, 642, 655, 656); Relationships (763, 764, 765)]. Additionally, the display screen shows menus, settings, and other information, and can be woken up with a button tap [Data: Entities (640, 641); Relationships (760, 761, 762)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Troubleshooting section provides systematic fault diagnosis\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The manual includes a 'Troubleshooting' chapter that helps users diagnose and resolve common problems such as lack of cooling, temperature anomalies, unusual noises, or water leaks. The chapter provides step-by-step solutions for checking power connections, thermostat settings, door seal integrity, and condenser cleanliness. It is divided into sub-sections for general issues and abnormal sounds, aiming to reduce unnecessary service calls [Data: Entities (31, 32, 33); Relationships (27, 28)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The SmartThings QR code facilitates app installation\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A QR code label located on the refrigerator's inner wall provides a direct link to download the SmartThings application. This simplifies the setup process for users, ensuring they can easily connect their refrigerator to the smart home platform. For support, users can contact st.service@samsung.com via email [Data: Entities (682, 702); Relationships (794, 808)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Operational practices affect food safety and energy efficiency\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Users are advised not to set temperatures lower than necessa